{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}{{ email.subject }} — {{ site_name }}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
    {# The way back to the member's page lives in the breadcrumb trail
       (design.md §7.3) — no « Retour » button here. #}
    {% include 'partials/page_header.html.twig' with {
        title: email.subject,
        subtitle: (email.not_sent|default(false) ? 'Non envoyée · ' ~ email.sent_at|french_date : 'Envoyé le ' ~ email.sent_at|french_date) ~ ' · ' ~ email.section_name,
    } only %}
    {# Nothing of it left for this member — every message in error, or no
       address it could go to. The content is still what was meant for
       them, so it is shown, under a sentence that says so. #}
    {% if email.not_sent|default(false) %}
        <div class="alert alert-warning" role="alert">
            Cet e-mail n'a pas pu être envoyé aux adresses de cet animé. Son contenu est reproduit ci-dessous.
        </div>
    {% endif %}
    {# A publipostage past its retention: the values that made this mail
       personal were erased on purpose (18 months — modules/mass_mail), and
       what is left is the template every recipient shared. Saying so is
       the only honest option — a reader shown a body still carrying its
       merge variables, with no explanation, reads it as a fault of the
       site rather than as a retention rule doing its job. #}
    {% if email.merge_purged %}
        <div class="alert alert-secondary" role="alert">
            Cet e-mail était personnalisé. Les valeurs qui vous concernaient ont été effacées depuis, comme le
            prévoit la durée de conservation : le texte ci-dessous est celui qui a servi de modèle, variables
            comprises.
        </div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="card">
        <div class="card-body">
            {{ email.body_html|raw }}
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
